namespace Interlocutor.AspNetCore;

using System;

/// <summary>
/// Marks <see cref="ResultExtensions"/> for source-generated <c>ToActionResult</c>/<c>ToMinimalApiResult</c>
/// overloads, one pair per <c>Outcome</c> case arity.
/// </summary>
/// <remarks>
/// <para>
/// Applying this attribute emits a second partial declaration adding the non-generic <c>Outcome</c> overload
/// and every <c>Outcome&lt;TSuccess, ...&gt;</c> arity's overload, generated by
/// <c>Interlocutor.Generator</c>'s <c>ResultExtensionsGenerator</c> - the same self-generation pattern
/// <c>Interlocutor.CommonKernel</c> uses for its own <c>Outcome</c> member generation via
/// <c>GenerateOutcomeMembersAttribute</c>. The reflective catch-all overload (for a hand-rolled
/// <see cref="Interlocutor.CommonKernel.ResultTypes.IOutcome"/> implementation) and the private
/// <see cref="OutcomeHttpMapping"/> rendering helpers stay hand-written in <see cref="ResultExtensions"/>
/// itself.
/// </para>
/// <para>
/// Internal, not part of this package's public extensibility surface - unlike <c>GenerateOutcomeMembersAttribute</c>,
/// there is no consumer-declared class this attribute is meant to be applied to; it exists purely so
/// <c>ResultExtensionsGenerator</c> has an attributed target to find in this project's own compilation.
/// </para>
/// </remarks>
[AttributeUsage(AttributeTargets.Class, Inherited = false, AllowMultiple = false)]
internal sealed class GenerateResultExtensionsAttribute : Attribute;
